c4de97d39014bb8","position":"1786440418147347001-4e91fdb7-a2ed-454e-8bd3-0fc06ca55e13"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation validation complete before review push. Held-out canonical/legacy oracle passed after one state-label follow-up; exact mutation reintroduced the wrong canonical gate label and returned RED, then restored GREEN. Full-suite preflight exposed the established string-patched _pause_exit_code seam had been renamed; existing selection/request held-outs were RED, restoring the old helper name made all four controls GREEN and preserves compatibility. Focused changed-surface suite is 62/62 green plus 4 seam controls; lint, typecheck, complexity, workflow lint, module-size (798/800), and diff checks pass. Renewed signed plan-review is PASS. Per operator instruction to push now and rely on CI, the 11,606-test make-test run was stopped green at 11%; Gerrit Verified remains the exhaustive gate and the ticket will not close before Verified +1.","timestamp":1786258252105030001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI held-out compatibility finding reproduced RED before repair: direct _resolve_held_lock callers received _Disposition.IN_FLIGHT instead of historical integer 3 in both live-holder and freed-then-acquire-lost cases. The implementation worker corrected the representation boundary without seeing or editing the held-out facade tests: the helper again returns 3, while main translates that semantic state through _Disposition.IN_FLIGHT so canonical sync exits 0 and legacy routes retain exit 3 plus their exact message. Post-fix GREEN evidence: the two previously failing nodes 2/2; focused canonical/legacy/direct-engine/workflow/selection suite 85/85; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; module remains 798/800. The CI RED is the defect-seeded mutation (the prior patchset had reintroduced the exact enum-leak mechanism); refactoring litmus passes because tests assert only observable return/exit/message behavior.","timestamp":1786259378817386001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence for the three previously unbanked repository-verifiable criteria:\n\n1. Numeric-consumer inventory (AC c07): a scoped search of tracked automation/deployment sources using `rg -n -i --glob \"*.yml\" --glob \"*.yaml\" --glob \"*.sh\" --glob \"*.py\" --glob \"*.service\" --glob \"*.timer\" --glob \"Jenkinsfile*\" \"(bridge|reconcil).{0,80}(3|4|75)|(3|4|75).{0,80}(bridge|reconcil)\" .github scripts infra` found no bridge/reconciler 3/4/75 handling in production workflows, scripts, probes, systemd units, or Jenkinsfiles. The remaining numeric-looking hits were unrelated issue ids, line/cadence comments, Jira priority probes, or Gerrit test-gate exit 3. `infra/systemd/rebar-autodeploy.service` and `.timer` contain no reconciler sentinel policy. The production workflow at `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:25-29` explicitly documents canonical preview/sync and 0/1/2. `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py:181-193` executes the production run block for 0/1/2 and asserts the old case whitelist is absent. Compatibility-only 3/4/75 uses remain deliberately in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, direct legacy tests, and documentation.\n\n2. Documentation (AC c08): `docs/exit-codes.md:29-54` defines canonical bridge 0/1/2, every benign state marker, retained legacy 3/4/75 translations, and the rolling-migration rationale. `docs/release-notes.md:29-46` records the same dual contract and states that systemd/Jenkins/scripts/checked-out workflows continue unchanged.\n\n3. Canonical constraint and continuity (AC c09): `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:55-66` defines one typed disposition with separate canonical and legacy exits; `:68-87` returns `canonical_exit` only for preview/sync and `legacy_exit` otherwise. All canonical exits in the enum are 0/1/2, while only legacy fields carry 3/4/75. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_lock_steal.py` exercise canonical and compatibility routes; the landed CI run 31300543302 passed the complete Python matrix. This is additive translation at the outer adapter, so old-vocabulary environments are not forced onto the new numeric contract.","timestamp":1786261395531856001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier evidence, bounded and exact:\n\nDocumentation proof: docs/exit-codes.md lines 29-54 define canonical bridge statuses 0/1/2, retained legacy reconcile statuses 3/4/75, and the rolling-migration guarantee. docs/release-notes.md lines 29-46 repeat both contracts and state that older workflows, systemd/Jenkins units, and scripts remain supported.\n\n[operator-attested] Test and gate proof: merged Gerrit change 1595 at 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 in GitHub Actions run 31300543302. That run passed the complete Python matrix, including test_reconcile_main.py, test_bridge_cli_heldout.py, test_lock_steal.py, test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py, public library facade tests, and MCP contract tests. The canonical and legacy routes therefore pass together at the exact ref used for completion certification.","timestamp":1786439799544158001}],"created_at":1786047485964649001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ec571d6c-35bc-469d-bcff-89f70e1e4d11","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4752-3afb-e8bd-448a"},{"link_uuid":"7d28a611-0a37-4393-8f70-9ecb3e353d5b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1104-93eb-6ce0-4a19"},{"link_uuid":"744008a5-751c-487d-a908-ae1300fd4877","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51"},{"link_uuid":"9f78e4b0-71cd-4606-94bd-7d02a25f2a01","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"42ec-05b9-b756-4d59"},{"link_uuid":"63fe81ca-62d8-4eb0-bfab-13f0cce4b358","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ef70-a14a-2446-484f"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCanonical bridge operations use conventional statuses: 0 for success or benign no-work/yield/paused states, 1 for operational failure, and 2 for invalid invocation/configuration. Legacy reconcile routes historically emit 3 for another live pass, 4 for the phase gate, and 75 for reschedule. The merged implementation centralizes semantic classification while retaining every legacy translation required by older workflows and environments.\n\nCanonical rebar bridge preview/sync and legacy rebar reconcile or direct python -m rebar_reconciler routes consume one typed disposition and differ only at the outer numeric adapter. Python and MCP bridge facades use the same core result; legacy Python rebar.reconcile and MCP reconcile continuity remains.\n\n## Exact contract\n\nCanonical preview/sync map converged, paused, in-flight, reschedule, and historical phase-gate states to 0; invalid invocation/configuration to 2; and operational failure to 1. Their state markers remain stable.\n\nLegacy CLI and direct-engine adapters map the same dispositions to the established 0/3/4/75/1/2 results with legacy messages and defaults. Older checked-out workflows, systemd/Jenkins units, scripts, and probes therefore continue to work. Retirement of the legacy codes is a separate future deprecation.\n\nThe production workflow uses the canonical route and no numeric whitelist. Preview remains non-mutating; sync preserves its existing mutation semantics; paused state still skips commit-and-push.\n\n## Verification\n\nRepository proof at merged ref 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d:\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py defines one disposition and separate canonical and legacy exits.\n- docs/exit-codes.md lines 29-54 and docs/release-notes.md lines 29-46 publish canonical 0/1/2, retained 3/4/75, and rolling-deployment continuity.\n- test_reconcile_main.py, test_bridge_cli_heldout.py, test_lock_steal.py, and test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py cover canonical/legacy subprocess and workflow behavior.\n- Public library and MCP contract suites cover both new bridge and retained reconcile facades.\n- The numeric-consumer census found no unclassified production 3/4/75 consumer; intentional uses remain only in legacy adapters, compatibility tests, and dual-contract documentation.\n\nNo new contention harness is required because the change classifies a result after existing lock/CAS seams and introduces no retry, cache, or composed write.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Canonical preview/sync emit only 0/1/2; benign dispositions exit 0 and no canonical adapter emits 3/4/75.\n- [x] Legacy reconcile CLI and direct-engine mode routes retain historical 3/4/75 translations, messages, and defaults.\n- [x] Canonical and legacy adapters consume one typed disposition, run the pass once, and preserve repository/ref effects.\n- [x] Python and MCP bridge and legacy consumers use the shared result boundary without a divergent whitelist.\n- [x] The production workflow uses canonical 0/1/2, has no old case whitelist, and preserves paused commit-skip behavior.\n- [x] Deployment, workflow, script, and probe consumers of 3/4/75 are migrated or explicitly classified as compatibility.\n- [x] Exit-code and release documentation publish both contracts and the rolling-migration guarantee.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Gerrit change 1595 and GitHub Actions run 31300543302 passed LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and the focused subprocess, workflow, library, and MCP continuity suites at merged ref 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"typed semantic disposition and route-specific canonical 0/1/2 versus legacy 3/4/75 process translation"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"consume shared disposition without a divergent canonical whitelist while preserving legacy adapter behavior"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"canonical bridge invocation and 0/1/2 handling with paused commit-skip"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_entry.py","reason":"core disposition and legacy direct-engine exit continuity"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py","reason":"canonical and legacy route parity across gate, lock, reschedule, and failure states"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py","reason":"real bridge/reconcile subprocess exit and state matrix"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py","reason":"canonical workflow simplification and legacy-workflow continuity fixture"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"canonical 0/1/2 and retained legacy translation contract"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"rolling migration and compatibility rationale"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1786435029130668001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1104-93eb-6ce0-4a19"],["depends_on","4752-3afb-e8bd-448a"],["depends_on","4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51"],["parent","2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3"],["relates_to","42ec-05b9-b756-4d59"],["relates_to","ef70-a14a-2446-484f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","parent_status_uuid":"d8a788fb-a42d-41df-9f65-3b30f89f6fa5","